## If the user explicitly approves a next run

Do not launch this unprompted.

- Stage B: collect `train500` (may reuse `train50` as the first 50; seed offset ≥ 100000). Confirm no seed shared with `val30` and no `HELDOUT_PAIRS`. At most two collectors, no GPU job at the same time. ~40–50 min with 4 processes is the old estimate; cap concurrency at 2 on this machine.
- Train: `--dataset-root data/datasets/train500 --output-dir checkpoints/stageB --steps 20000 --warmup-steps 500`, `save_freq 2500`, `val_every 500`, `min_steps 4000`, `patience_evals 6`. Ask the user before changing the sleep timeout. Resume is not wired; add `--resume-from` only if a run actually dies.
- Then `eval_checkpoints.py` on the same val20 seeds, plus `best/` on 50 fresh seeds (`--n-episodes 50 --seed 5000`) that are not in train or the val20 list and are not held-out pairs.
- Held-out pair / held-out template / same-seed text-swap tests come after that, not before.

Likely reasons the 50-demo gate failed, if the user asks: frozen vision encoder, too little data, grasp needs centimeter precision. Report numbers; do not start a retrain to test those unless asked.
